# Citation metadata for TractorJAX (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# Read by GitHub ("Cite this repository") and by Zenodo when a release is
# archived through the GitHub integration.  Keep `version` in step with
# tractor_jax/version.py and with the release tag; set `date-released` when
# the release is cut.  A methods paper is in preparation: add a
# `preferred-citation` block here once it has a DOI, so that citations of the
# software resolve to the paper.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use TractorJAX in your research, please cite it using the metadata
  in this file.  A methods paper is in preparation and will be added as the
  preferred citation when published.
type: software
title: TractorJAX
abstract: >-
  GPU-accelerated, JAX-based reimplementation of the catalog-forced
  photometry mode of The Tractor.  Source positions and morphologies are
  frozen at their reference-catalog values and the fluxes of every source in
  a cutout are solved jointly in one weighted least-squares solve, with
  optional eigenvalue-floor, external-prior (Gaussian) and L1 regularization
  and per-source uncertainties validated against simulation truth.  Developed
  for SPHEREx spectrophotometry.  TractorJAX is a derivative work of The
  Tractor and is distributed under the same license.
authors:
  - family-names: Bahk
    given-names: Hyeonguk
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0002-9878-1126
    affiliation: >-
      Astronomy Program, Department of Physics and Astronomy, Seoul National
      University
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: https://github.com/hbahk/tractor-jax
url: https://tractor-jax.readthedocs.io/
license: GPL-2.0-only
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - forced photometry
  - deblending
  - photometric redshifts
  - SPHEREx
  - JAX
  - GPU
references:
  - type: software
    title: "The Tractor: Probabilistic astronomical source detection and measurement"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lang
        given-names: Dustin
      - family-names: Hogg
        given-names: David W.
      - family-names: Mykytyn
        given-names: David
    year: 2016
    repository-code: https://github.com/dstndstn/tractor
    notes: "Astrophysics Source Code Library record ascl:1604.008; TractorJAX is a derivative work."
